      "items": [
        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "1. Given each storefront is configured in BM, when accessed, then the correct default locale is assigned per the storefront configuration table (Confluence: 03 Storefronts).\n2. Given the EU domestic storefront, when configured in BM, then all 4 language locales are active: /en-eu/, /fr-eu/, /it-eu/, /es-eu/.\n3. Given the EU international storefront, when configured, then the /en-ch/ locale is active.\n4. Given all storefronts, when the URL structure is configured, then paths match the agreed locale structure: AU (/), UK (/uk/), US (/us/), US International (/en-ca/), ME (/en-ae/), HK (/hk/), EU domestic (/en-eu/, /fr-eu/, /it-eu/, /es-eu/), EU International (/en-ch/).\n5. Given any storefront locale, when translated content is unavailable for a customer's selected locale, then the storefront falls back to English.\n6. Given AU, US, ME, and HK storefronts, when configured, then a single English locale is active with no additional language options.\n7. Given the EU domestic storefront, when a customer selects a language locale, then that selection is reflected in the storefront URL.",
          "to_string": "1. Given each storefront is configured in BM, when accessed, then the correct default locale is assigned per the storefront configuration table.\n2. Given the EU domestic storefront, when configured in BM, then all 4 language locales are active: /en-eu/, /fr-eu/, /it-eu/, /es-eu/.\n3. Given the EU international storefront, when configured, then the /en-ch/ locale is active.\n4. Given all storefronts, when the URL structure is configured, then paths match the agreed locale structure.",
          "from_id": "",
          "to_id": ""
        }
      ],
