    {
      "items": [
        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "As a Site Admin,\n\nI want to configure the correct locales and URL structure for each of the 8 Zimmermann storefronts in SFCC Business Manager,\n\nso that each storefront serves the correct language(s) and operates on the correct URL path per market.\n\nThis story is split out from SFCC-48 (8 Storefronts Setup) to allow storefront creation to proceed independently while locale and URL configuration is finalised. It covers locale assignment per storefront, EU multi-language locale setup, and the URL path structure across all 11 active locales.",
          "to_string": "*As a* Site Admin,\n\n*I want* to configure the correct locales and URL structure for each of the 8 Zimmermann storefronts in SFCC Business Manager,\n\n*so that* each storefront serves the correct language(s) and operates on the correct URL path per market.\n\n----\n\nThis story is split out from SFCC-48 (8 Storefronts Setup) to allow storefront creation to proceed independently while locale and URL configuration is finalised. It covers locale assignment per storefront, EU multi-language locale setup, and the URL path structure across all 8 storefronts."
        }
      ],
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-14T12:39:38.103000+10:00"
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "to_string": "1. Given each storefront is configured in BM, when accessed, then the correct default locale is assigned per the storefront configuration table (Confluence: 03 Storefronts).\n2. Given the EU domestic storefront, when configured in BM, then all 4 language locales are active: /en-eu/, /fr-eu/, /it-eu/, /es-eu/.\n3. Given the EU international storefront, when configured, then the /en-ch/ locale is active.\n4. Given all storefronts, when the URL structure is configured, then paths match the agreed locale structure: AU (/), UK (/uk/), US (/us/), US International (/en-ca/), ME (/en-ae/), HK (/hk/), EU domestic (/en-eu/, /fr-eu/, /it-eu/, /es-eu/), EU International (/en-ch/).\n5. Given any storefront locale, when translated content is unavailable for a customer's selected locale, then the storefront falls back to English.\n6. Given AU, US, ME, and HK storefronts, when configured, then a single English locale is active with no additional language options.\n7. Given the EU domestic storefront, when a customer selects a language locale, then that selection is reflected in the storefront URL.",
          "to_id": ""
        },
        {
          "field": "Dependency",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "to_string": "@Jasmijn Tsang: REG-043 — open discussion noted in FRs around updating domestic locales to include language prefix (e.g. en-us, en-au). Confirm whether this is in scope or enhancement log before development begins.\nDepends on SFCC-48 (8 Storefronts Setup) — storefronts must exist in BM before locale/URL configuration can be applied.",
          "to_id": ""
        }
      ],
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
