{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "253362177",
    "title": "04.5 Storefronts",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/253362177",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 21,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "This page defines the eight storefront configurations to be set up in Salesforce Commerce Cloud (SFCC). It provides a quick reference for currency, tax handling, checkout routing, and supported locales across domestic and international storefront experiences.\n\n**Purpose:** Use this page as the baseline reference when configuring sites, locale mappings, pricing, taxation, and checkout behavior in SFCC and connected services such as Global-e and Avalara.\n\nStorefront configuration table\n------------------------------\n\n| **Storefront Name** | **SFCC Site ID** | **Default Currency** | **Customer List** | **Taxation** | **Locale(s)** | **URL Path** | **Default Timezone** | **Product Catalogue** | **Pricebook** | **Inventory List** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Australia (AU) | ZimmermannAU | AUD | Zimmermann Global List | Gross | en\\_AU | /en-au | AEST/AEDT — UTC+10/+11 | AU Storefront Catalogue | `au-aud-list-prices` | AU Inventory |\n| US Domestic | ZimmermannUS | USD | Zimmermann Global List | Net | en\\_US | N/A, root URL  (/us will be redirected to root URL) | EST/EDT — UTC-5/-4 | US Storefront Catalogue | `us-usd-list-prices` | US Inventory |\n| US International | ZimmermannUSIntl | USD | Zimmermann Global List | Net | en\\_CA | /en-ca | EST/EDT — UTC-5/-4 | US Storefront Catalogue | `usintl-usd-list-prices` | US Inventory |\n| UK (Domestic) | ZimmermannUK | GBP | Zimmermann Global List | Gross | en\\_GB | /uk | GMT/BST — UTC+0/+1 | UK Storefront Catalogue | `uk-gbp-list-prices` | UK Inventory |\n| EU (Domestic) | ZimmermannEU | EUR | Zimmermann Global List | Gross | en\\_FR (default)  fr\\_FR  es\\_ES  it\\_IT | /en-eu  /fr-eu  /es-eu  /it-eu | CET/CEST — UTC+1/+2 | EU Domestic Storefront Catalogue | `eu-eur-list-prices` | EU Domestic Inventory |\n| EU (International) | ZimmermannEUIntl | EUR | Zimmermann Global List | Gross | en\\_CH | /en-ch | CET/CEST — UTC+1/+2 | EU International Storefront Catalogue | `euintl-eur-list-prices` | EU International Inventory |\n| Hong Kong (International) | ZimmermannHK | USD | Zimmermann Global List | Gross | en\\_HK | /hk | HKT — UTC+8 | HK Storefront Catalogue | `hk-usd-list-prices` | Hong Kong Inventory |\n| Middle East (International) | ZimmermannME | EUR | Zimmermann Global List | Gross | en\\_AE | /en-ae | GST — UTC+4 | ME Storefront Catalogue | `me-eur-list-prices` | Middle East Inventory |\n\nDefinitions of the different settings in the storefront:\n\n**Default Currency:** This is the default currency SFCC uses as a baseline for everything in that storefront. Also, the storefront's pricebook aligns to this currency. It is also the fallback system - what currency gets displayed when no other currency context is detected.\n\n**Customer List:** We create one global customer list (Zimmermann Global List) so that all customers who have an account can log in on all storefronts.\n\n**Taxation:** In SFCC this is essentially a binary setting per storefront — **Gross** or **Net** — configured in Business Manager.\n\n**Gross:** Prices stored and displayed in the system already include tax. What the customer sees on the PLP, PDP is what they pay. Tax amount can still be calculated and specified at checkout.\n\n**Net:** Prices stored in the system are exclusive of tax. Tax is calculated by Avalara at checkout and added on top, making the final price higher than the displayed product price.\n\n**Locales:** Locales in SFCC are the combination of language + region (e.g. en-AU, fr-FR, it-IT) and they drive a surprising amount beyond just language translation. Here's what they can control: content and language, data formatting (currency, date/time), SEO.\n\n**Default timezone:** The default timezone is the timezone SFCC uses as the system clock reference for that storefront. It's set per storefront in BM. Mostly important for promotions and campaigns start date/time.\n\n**Product Catalogue:** In SFCC you have one master catalogue that holds all products, attributes, and the master product hierarchy. Then each storefront gets assigned a storefront catalogue which is essentially a subset/view of the master — it controls which products and categories are visible and navigable on that specific site.\n\n**Pricebook:** The default pricebook per storefront - the pricebook SFCC falls back to when no other pricebook context can be determined for that session (RRP list pricebook for the storefronts currency).\n\n**Inventory list:** In SFCC, an inventory list is a named record that holds stock availability per SKU — on-hand quantities, whether a product is in stock, backorder settings etc. Like pricebooks, you assign one to a storefront as the default. SFCC looks at that inventory list to determine whether a product is available to purchase on that site.\n\nStores per Storefront\n---------------------\n\nImplementation notes\n--------------------\n\n* **Default language:** the fallback language if no locale match is found. English is the site-wide fallback across all storefronts.\n* **Domestic SFCC storefronts:** AU, UK, EU Domestic, and US Domestic follow the core SFCC checkout flow.\n* **US Domestic storefront:** Uses SFCC for domestic checkout, with tax calculated as tax exclusive through Avalara at checkout.\n* **US International storefront:** Routing is handled through Global-e for international customers.\n* **EU Domestic:** Supports multiple locale variants and country-specific VAT-inclusive pricing behavior.\n* **Global-e managed storefronts:** EU International, HK, and ME rely on Global-e for tax and checkout handling.\n\n**Important:** \"Global-e only\" indicates that checkout is not expected to run through a native SFCC domestic checkout flow for that storefront. Ensure routing, localization, and handoff behavior are aligned during implementation.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f3db",
    "page_width": "max"
  }
}"}

